.TH SDL_PenID 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_PenID \- SDL pen instance IDs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pen.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef Uint32 SDL_PenID;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Zero is used to signify an invalid/null device\[char46]
.PP
These show up in pen events when SDL sees input from them\[char46] They remain consistent as long as SDL can recognize a tool to be the same pen; but if a pen\(aqs digitizer table is physically detached from the computer, it might get a new ID when reconnected, as SDL won\(aqt know it\(aqs the same device\[char46]
.PP
These IDs are only stable within a single run of a program; the next time a program is run, the pen\(aqs ID will likely be different, even if the hardware hasn\(aqt been disconnected, etc\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

